description: How work on Beru is verified before it is called done
alwaysApply: true
---

# The gate

`./scripts/qa.sh` is the only definition of "it builds". Run it before saying a
change is finished. It runs static guards, `xcodegen generate`, a build, the
tests, then prints `docs/QA-CHECKLIST.md`.

- `--static` for guards only, `--fast` to skip tests.
- The guards are a ratchet against `scripts/qa-baseline.txt`. A count going up
  fails the gate. After deliberately removing debt, run `--update-baseline` and
  commit the lower numbers in the same commit.
- Never raise a baseline number to make the gate pass.

# One change per pass

State the blast radius before editing: which files, and which screens can break
as a consequence. Then make that one change. Do not fold an unrelated cleanup,
rename, or "while I'm here" fix into the same pass.

# Hand back a scoped manual check

Automated checks cannot see the screen, and the user's time is the scarce
resource. End every change by naming the specific screens and states to click,
drawn from the section of `docs/QA-CHECKLIST.md` that matches what changed.
Never ask for a full-app regression sweep.

# Do not do these unprompted

- Bump `MARKETING_VERSION` / `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` in `project.yml`
- Create a git tag, push, or trigger the release workflow
- Build a DMG
- Commit, unless the user asked for a commit

# Regressions this project has already paid for

Before touching these, re-read why they broke:

- Reading Keychain on view appearance caused repeating system password prompts.
  Provider keys go through `SettingsStore`'s cache, never `KeychainStore.shared`
  directly, and never for a provider that has no key.
- Unthrottled progress updates on a shared `@Observable` froze the Settings
  window. Throttle high-frequency publishes.
- Animations attached high in the panel tree re-laid-out the whole window on a
  tab change. Scope `.animation` to the element that changes.
